      "message": "Fixed. `slugify` no longer produces repeated or edge dashes.\n\n**The bug:** in `slug/core.py`, every non-alphanumeric character was turned into its own `-`. So `\"Hello  World\"` (two spaces) gave `hello--world`, and `\"a -- b\"` gave `a----b`. Leading and trailing separators were also kept.\n\n**The fix:** the final line now splits on `-`, drops the empty pieces, and rejoins:\n\n```python\nreturn \"-\".join(part for part in \"\".join(out).split(\"-\") if part)\n```\n\n**Confirmation:** I ran a quick one-off check, not the test suite. Results:\n- `\"Hello World\"` → `hello-world`\n- `\"Hello  World\"` → `hello-world`\n- `\"a -- b\"` → `a-b`\n- `\"  --x--  \"` → `x`\n- `\"ABC\"` → `abc`\n- `\"\"` → `\"\"`\n\nI did not run `pytest` and did not commit. Your current `test_core.py` cases still hold by inspection.",
